  "answer": "Based on official metrics and customer success reports, NovaLearn should prioritize the **regulated mid-market and enterprise customer segments**.\n\nThe evidence clearly shows these segments are the most successful and capital-efficient. Mid-market and enterprise accounts combined generate **83.8% of recurring revenue** [NL-016#NL-016-S03]. They exhibit substantially lower monthly churn—**2.1%** for mid-market and **1.3%** for enterprise, compared to **4.8%** for SMB [NL-012#NL-012-S09]. They also drive higher expansion revenue ($155,000 combined vs $18,000 for SMB) and report significantly higher NPS [NL-012#NL-012-S09], with segment NPS scores of **47** for mid-market and **52** for enterprise versus **31** for SMB [NL-012#NL-012-S08]. Unit economics reinforce this: the enterprise segment has an LTV:CAC ratio of **16.0x**, compared to **8.3x** for SMB [NL-016#NL-016-S03].\n\nFurther, the strategic shift is explicitly stated, with leadership moving outbound sales focus entirely away from SMBs because smaller startups show weak long-term retention compared to regulated mid-market and enterprise companies [NL-016#NL-016-S03]. The common denominator among highest-performing accounts is regulatory compliance, where NovaLearn has a distinct competitive advantage due to verified, citation-backed answers [NL-016#NL-016-S03].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
